# AGENTS.md

Guidance for AI coding agents working in `{{name}}`, a Discord bot built with
[`@wolfstar/http-framework`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@wolfstar/http-framework). It receives interactions over
HTTP{{#if gateway}} and gateway events over a WebSocket (`@wolfstar/plugin-gateway`){{/if}}.

## Commands

- `npm run dev` — build, run and restart the bot on changes (`stars dev`). Add `-- --no-tui` for plain line output,
  which is what a non-interactive shell gets anyway.
{{#if typescript}}
- `npm run build` — build once (`stars build`).
{{/if}}
- `npm start` — run the built bot.
- `npx stars doctor` — check the runtime, the credentials and the generated files. Run it first when something is off.
- `npx stars info --json` — the resolved configuration.
- `npx stars commands diff` — what a deploy would change on Discord. `npx stars commands deploy --yes` deploys.
{{#if i18n}}
- `npm run generate:i18n` — regenerate the i18next types after editing `src/locales/`.
{{/if}}
{{#if testing}}
- `npm test` — run the tests (vitest).
{{/if}}

## Layout

- `src/main.*` — the entry: creates the client, loads the pieces, starts listening.
- `src/commands/` — one file per application command. A command registers its own builder
  (`@RegisterCommand(...)` or `registerApplicationCommands`) and answers in `chatInputRun`.
- `src/interaction-handlers/` — buttons, select menus and modals, matched by custom id.
- `src/listeners/` — client event listeners.
- `src/lib/` — shared code{{#unless vite}}, auto-imported by `stars` (see `.stars/imports.d.ts`){{/unless}}.
{{#if i18n}}
- `src/locales/<locale>/` — translations. Keys are typed: never build a key from a variable.
{{/if}}
- `stars.config.*` — the only build and dev configuration. There is no separate bundler config.
- `.stars/` — generated by `stars prepare`. Never edit it, and do not commit it.

{{#if vite}}
The project is bundled into one file, so there is no `commands` directory at runtime: import every new piece in
`src/main.*` and load it with `container.stores.loadPiece`.

{{/if}}
## Rules

- Secrets live in `.env` (`DISCORD_TOKEN`, `DISCORD_PUBLIC_KEY`, `DISCORD_CLIENT_ID`). Never print or commit them.
- Call Discord through `container.rest`, not `fetch`: it handles rate limits and authentication.
- An interaction must be answered within 3 seconds: `reply()`, or `defer()` first and `edit()` later. `edit()` before
  either one fails.
{{#if tunnel}}
- `stars dev` opens a public cloudflared tunnel to the bot (`dev.tunnel` in `stars.config`). Its URL changes on every
  run; it is the application's interactions endpoint only while the session lasts.
{{/if}}
- Changing a command's builder (name, description, options) changes what Discord has to be told. `stars dev` asks
  before it redeploys; outside it, use `stars commands deploy`.
- Do not start a long-running `npm run dev` to check a change: build{{#if testing}} and run the tests{{/if}} instead.

